      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I hope this gets resolved. I love playing VRChat, but lately, I’ve been getting disconnected so often that I was forced to spend money on a VPN and Virtual Desktop to fix this issue. On top of that, I have to spend around $8 monthly just to keep the VPN running. It’s frustrating to have high ping and keep getting disconnected, especially since I spend around $40 on 1GB of internet, and due to the lack of local servers in Brazil, I can’t even enjoy a simple gameplay session.\n\nAdditionally, I currently use VRPlus. $10 might be cheap for people earning in euros or dollars, but for Brazilians, it’s quite a lot. I believe that if the price were reduced to $4.99, it would be much fairer, allowing people who already subscribe to maintain their membership for much longer and encouraging many more Brazilian players to support the game they love. We all hope for some recognition from the VRChat team.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
